let's get the Trump administration  perspective tonight on the latest polls  the Bolton book other topics Kellyanne  Conway is counselor to the president  Kellyanne thanks for being here  good evening Bret I want to start out  with this this book the administration  has been fighting to prevent it from  being released going to court over it  the John Bolton is now out doing  interviews he'll be as I mentioned on  special report next week he is saying  and it's in the book that the president  from what he saw in the room is unfit  for office what do you say to that well  a couple things when people do tell-all  books I'd prefer that they tell us all  what they accomplished in those  positions so I've known John for a long  time served alongside of him in the  White House for all 17 months he was  there and I much of his national  security accomplishments that happened  and there are many in the Donald Trump  presidency happened before he got there  or after he left the capture of al  Baghdadi soleimani sanctioning the ICC  getting the Afghan troop withdrawal down  to almost half and and with the target I  talked to our national security  administrator today or director today  Robert ambassador Robert O'Brien said  we'll probably get to zero by May of  2021 so many of these things have  happened since he's gone and I like when  people tell us all that they  accomplished I also would point out and  others have done this that ambassador  Bolton John Bolton had many nice things  to say about the president complimentary  but I think the one that's most  important to some of the allegations in  his book is what he said in the White  House briefing room he said quote since  2017 January 2017 President Trump has  been taking decisive action against  election meddling and interference in  his book he claims that the president is  asking President Xi to help him win  farmers in the Midwest this makes no  sense I personally have had private  meetings with John Bolton where we've  discussed Chinese fentanyl for example  since I run the drug crisis at the White  House and he never said to me gee Kelly  and we have a problem with getting the  Chinese pencil analogs scheduled as  president she has promised because after  all the president president Chavez asked  and helped in the election so some of  this smacks people's brand new  information and false as well I know  you're in  ruin him next week and I would just  remind you that and everybody who's  watching that Bolton decide these books  are never fact checked so you  interviewed James Comey in December of  2019 or 2018 and he lied to you he lied  to you and you called him on it and he  was it was revealed that he lied to you  he didn't know he said he doesn't know  that the Democrats funded the sales  hacia you said what do you mean you  don't know what he said I still don't  know it is the fact the Republicans did  you said no you correctly said no they  didn't and it turned out when we saw the  FISA warrants that an honor about  October 12 2016 he had been briefed  about that and then he included that  unverified dossier which is a French  word for a load of bunk sure I'm in the  briefing sure you're in presidential  you're saying that in this book there  are lies and that his perception is not  accurate here but yet lake says Bouldin  himself is a legendary note-taker who  keeps a detailed record of his life one  of his former staffers told me this is  Eli Lake that Bolton takes notes on what  he had for breakfast  also if Bolton's book is all lies why  would the White House try to block its  publication and claim he is revealing  classified information Bolton's account  of the trip I didn't say that  because it's devastating it's  devastating excuse me I'm sorry there's  a little delay Brett I didn't mean to  interrupt so no I didn't say it was all  lies what I said was it's important to  put it all in the perspective of the  tenure that he had there what has  happened since he left and the fact that  he didn't raise any of this in a  meaningful way while he was there and I  will tell you that those of us who do  work there are duty-bound we took a note  of the Constitution we work for the  country we are duty-bound to give advice  and try to brief the President and  breanne and work with other members of  the cabinet of the senior staff the  outside world Congress certainly on any  number of issues to try to improve this  country that's what we're trying to do  there so I know he's a note-taker I  wouldn't miss it firsthand and all I'm  saying is I think we need context here  that ambassador dabble and as somebody  who was crediting the president not just  for being decisive  around the globe on many different on  many different actions in fact he's on  tape saying that many times but the one  that really caught my eye today when I  went back through some of it was him in  the White House press briefing room  saying that for the entire presidency of  Donald Trump President Trump has taken  quote decisive action against election  meddling and interference and does  anybody believe that the president asked  President Xi to help him win the  election it's so ridiculous in fact  ambassador delight Heiser was asked it  with no warning yesterday by Senator  Menendez and hearing about other issues  and ambassador white Heiser was under  oath and immediately said immediately  spontaneous he said never happened I was  there and reported so ambassador white  Heiser is saying this is in the room  that where it didn't happen so I think  look these other a lot of books out  there that turn out to have tremendous  falsities I don't know why these books  aren't fact checked even names are wrong  dates are wrong sometimes quotes are  attributed to somebody positively and  somebody else said it they weren't even  there so I do I'm glad you'll have a  chance to interview him I think that's  important I think the departed justice  has made clear it's unusual to release a  book like this while people that you  work with are still doing their jobs and  while the president is still in office  that's the unusual part well other  people have done it we had former  secretary Bob gates who wrote a book  about the Obama administration while he  was still in office other people have  done it but you're right to be this  pointed in this direct there are a lot  of things that are getting picked yet  picked up I want to quickly I only have  a few seconds is this rally happening in  Tulsa 100 percent it's not going to be  moved outside it's it's definitely going  to happen the information I have from  the campaign is that it's happening and  I think people want to get out there and  express their beliefs peaceably you've  seen people do it through protests  through peaceful protests and otherwise  and you're seeing you're going to see  people whether it's in Tulsa or elsewise  Brett they want to participate in our  great democracy also I also would say  that Oklahoma I believe is in phase  three and so you can have gatherings of  a certain number in doors and I know  that people are adhering to the  protocols but we can't pick and choose  who can be where wearing a mask or not  based on our politics based on whether  some people think that folks are  irredeemable and deplorable they have  the same rights as anybody else to  peacefully assemble peaceably assemble  under our Constitution and I think it's  important that they do that also I know  you were talking a lot about the poll  since I'm was a pollster for many years  yeah respectfully we never did one  single national poll when I was campaign  manager of Trump ends 2016 why they're a  colossal waste of time and money  statewide polls are really the gold  standard David Plouffe another  successful campaign manager for  President Obama backed me up on that  yesterday and said these are like 50  different governor's races  state-by-state  let's look at those statewide polls and  I think the polls in the States right  now are about where I would expect them  to be depending on the poll with Trump  invited both under 50% and most of those  statewide polls and within a few points  of each other I saw that in 2016 the day  Donald Trump asked me to become the  campaign manager in August and we saw  they were both under 50 they were within  a couple points of each other and then  you go into the state-by-state we know  President Trump and vice president pence  are going to spend more time out in  those swing states then Joe Biden ever  Ken and they will be connecting directly  talking about the proxy port of the  Trump administration and laying out the  vision for the next four years well  that's definitely a national poll out  tonight but we do swing state polls and  battleground state polls as well  Kellyanne we appreciate your time thank  you Brad

